[http://www.lojban.org/tiki/cultural+gismu|It's been said before.] [http://www.lojban.org/tiki/cultural+fu'ivla|More than once.] These cultures gotta get out of our gismu.

Instead of bothering with poorly defined cultural identities, ku'ufu'ivla should first focus on 'easier' domains. That is, select candidates according to internationally defined and regulated entities. Suggestions below:

*1) Languages, according to [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_ISO_639-1_codes|ISO codes]; 
following the precedent of approximating the native pronunciation (a conventional cmene) and then converting it into a suitable CCVVCV fi'uvla.
*2) Political Territories, according to something like [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Countries_of_the_world|this list]; 
using the pronunciation of the country's name in the most populous official language.
*3) more?

The above lists do all the preparations, formatted lists of standard, acknowledged languages with the native name and pronunciation. Let's transfer them into tikitables and then get this over with!